r body incredibly flexible and elastic.  Her muscles, tendons, ligaments and bones were so soft and pliable that she could bend and fold them in any direction without any discomfort or damage.  For example, she can split her legs 360 degrees, bend her back at any point, or bend her foot in half.  Her nervous system was also adapted to her flexibility so that she did not experience pain or overload from her movements.  She always felt good and comfortable in her body.  She likes to almost always make movements and poses that seem impossible for ordinary people.  She is also incredibly agile, and often likes to walk on her hands.  She does this most of the time at home.  If she does not walk on her hands, then she tries to walk on bent toes, and almost never walks at home just on a full foot.  She also loves and tries to use her legs instead of her arms.  She loves her feet so much that from time to time she can touch her toe to various parts of her head or put her whole foot on her head, and sometimes kiss her feet.  She is tough enough to walk a kilometer on her hands and hardly get tired of it.  She also knows how to do push-ups in a triple fold, without getting tired.  She is 16 years old.  She is ambidexter.  She has short brown hair, and a very pretty face with a cute little nose and big blue eyes.  She lives alone in an apartment.  Her parents send her money and she doesn't work yet.\n\nНапиши рассказ, как она на спор бегала на руках по стадиону и отжималась\n\nPlease add more detail in that story\n\nWirte a story please how she pull ups and play with her legs at the same time, like doing splits and etc..  Please, add as much as you can details and discribe in details all her movements\n\nOk, now you are fiction storyteller. While you write a story, you can to image something new about person you write and write it. Plus, you can create a new characters and put them in a story for more live, and can create and write some situation, that complement original idea